ing for the project so additionally a capital improvement plan and a capital budget the capital budget associated with it are different than an operating budget in that the projects very often continue from one year to the next until the project is completed so tonight we're going to give you a high level overview of the projects in the capital improvement plan from 20 from 2026 to 2030 the totals associated for the capital budget with that plan and then some of these projects included in the plan have already started but continue beyond the end of this year beyond the end of 2025 and some of the projects won't start until later in the plan some starting as late as 2030. so as i mentioned by next monday we'll publish the full capital improvement plan listing all of the projects and the budget for each broken down for each year from 2026 to 2030. and again i'll review the schedule for the process at the end of the of the presentation here all right so i'm going to start tonight with the total costs and the funding sources in the plan so there's 142 projects included in the plan for a total of approximately 299.1 million or about 300 million we have the projects in this chart divided into six different sections but three of the sections the parks the pw public works admin and the streets are all included in the general fund and then the other three sections sewer stormwater management and water are labeled based on the enterprise fund that they're associated with so the the colors are a little hard to see on this screen but the sewer is the orange and the water is the dark blue and you can see that those two sections have the biggest need they make up approximately two-thirds of the costs this is not unusual for water and sewer facilities since those utilities rely so heavily on major infrastructure to function properly however it does create some challenges as we've talked about already for containing debt debt payment costs and keeping fees reasonable as we try to e